# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where git's core.autocrlf=true checks
# files out as CRLF while storing them as LF. That is invisible until a tool
# writes a file directly (the fixture downloaders, prettier) and git then
# reports a whole tree as modified over line endings alone.
#
# Settle it here instead of relying on each machine's git config: normalize
# every text file to LF in the repository *and* in the working tree. The
# repository already stores LF, so this changes no committed content — it only
# stops CRLF from reappearing in the working tree.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Bash runs the hooks in .claude/settings.json; CRLF would break the shebang.
*.sh            text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts genuinely need CRLF.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Generated; not worth reviewing in diffs.
package-lock.json  -diff linguist-generated=true

# SEC fixtures are evidence, not source: they are downloaded verbatim and their
# expected.json values were verified against those exact bytes. Mark them so
# diffs stay readable but nobody reformats them.
fixtures/**     -diff
